<UserControl x:Class="Bws.Gui.StatusRow"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             Focusable="False"
             IsTabStop="False">

    <!--
        WHAT THE WINDOW ADMITS ABOUT AN ANSWER, AND THE ONE WAY OUT IT OFFERS.

        Two lines and never more than two. The count moved up beside the box it answers - complaint
        8 - and so, on 2026-09-23, did everything about the QUESTION: its mistakes and what its answer
        could not judge stand under the search box now (UX-GUI-002 and 009). What is left here is
        about the WINDOW - the session's rights, the folded copies, the list holding still - and,
        on the second line, what the window tried and could not do.

        A UserControl SINCE 2026-08-25 BECAUSE THE MARKUP RATCHET ASKED, and it is the fourth part
        of this window to leave the same way, after ScopeBar, SearchRow and FilterRow. The seam is
        the one those three established: MainWindow.xaml is what the window IS, and a row with a
        subject of its own lives in a file named for that subject. This row's subject is the truth
        about an answer.

        WHAT ASKED FOR IT WAS ONE ATTRIBUTE. The notice line had no automation id, so nothing
        outside the process could read the one place this window says an answer is incomplete -
        `A11` put a new admission there and there was no instrument that could see it. The comment
        explaining that could not be added to a file already standing on the ceiling, which is the
        ratchet doing exactly what it is for.

        Focusable and IsTabStop are off because a UserControl IS a ContentControl and a
        ContentControl is BOTH BY DEFAULT. Without them this row is a tab stop that does nothing,
        in front of the button it holds. `docs/10` trap 8.

        IT INHERITS THE WINDOW'S DataContext rather than being handed one, unlike the details and
        plan panels. Those are bound to one object so that nothing in them can reach the list - this
        one reads Says, which hangs off the model, and narrowing it to Says would leave the row
        unable to grow the second sentence it may one day owe.
    -->
    <StackPanel Margin="{StaticResource MarginAboveStatus}">

        <!--
            THE ONE SENTENCE IN THIS WINDOW THAT HAS A WAY OUT, since 2026-08-25. Everything
            else this line says is a fact about an answer - a session without administrator
            rights is a state somebody can leave, and until now the window said so and offered
            nothing. `docs/11` section 6 names that as this window's weakest heuristic.

            The button asks WHICH FACT rather than whether the line is empty: most of what is
            said here is about the query, and a way out offered beside a sentence about
            signatures would be a control that means nothing.
        -->
        <Grid>
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

            <!--
                ITS OWN AutomationId SINCE 2026-08-25, AND THE GAP WAS FOUND BY NEEDING IT. The
                count line beside the search box has had one for weeks and this line never did,
                so nothing outside the process could read the one place the window admits what
                an answer is not - and `A11` put a new admission here on the day it was wanted.
                A sentence no instrument can see is a sentence only a person staring at the
                window can check, which is the fifth time this window has paid for that lesson.
            -->
            <!--
                THREE RUNS RATHER THAN ONE Text, SINCE 2026-09-15 - point 8(d) of `docs/11` 2.14.
                The sentence about folded instances NAMED the switch ("Show every instance lists
                them on their own") and now the name IS the switch: the words in the middle are a
                link that presses it. The line stays one string in the model - Says.Notice is the
                three pieces joined - so the trigger below, the tests and the automation name
                all read what they always read. The pieces are written WITHOUT whitespace between
                the tags on purpose: XAML folds the space between inline elements into one real
                space, which would have put an indent in front of a line whose first piece is
                empty. The spacing is in the pieces themselves, cut by Sentences.

                THE LINK IS SWITCHED OFF WHEN IT IS EMPTY, or an invisible Hyperlink would be a
                Tab stop that does nothing - trap 8 of `docs/10`, one element down. Its colour is
                the line's own.

                FOUR RUNS SINCE 2026-09-23 - UX-GUI-009. The first is the sentence about rights, in
                red on its own, and the line after it is in the notice colour. What this line says
                about the ANSWER - reading in progress, fields nobody could read, an expression that
                ran out of time - moved under the search box, where the question is (SearchRow.xaml).
                What stays is about the window: rights, the folded copies and the list holding still.
                The line keeps its AutomationId and still starts with the rights sentence, because
                tools/gui-probe/errands.ps1 and tools/window-journey/journey.ps1 read it (backlog 429).
            -->
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0"
                       AutomationProperties.AutomationId="noticeLine"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap"><Run Text="{Binding Says.NoticeRights, Mode=OneWay}" Foreground="{StaticResource MeaningRejected}" /><Run Text="{Binding Says.NoticeBeforeLink, Mode=OneWay}" /><Hyperlink x:Name="FoldLink" AutomationProperties.AutomationId="noticeLink"
                                                                                                          Style="{StaticResource NoticeLink}"
                                                                                                          IsEnabled="{Binding Says.NoticeHasLink}"
                                                                                                          Click="ShowEveryInstance"><Run Text="{Binding Says.NoticeLink, Mode=OneWay}" /></Hyperlink><Run Text="{Binding Says.NoticeAfterLink, Mode=OneWay}" />
                <TextBlock.Style>
                    <Style TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource NoticeText}">
                        <Style.Triggers>
                            <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding Says.NoticeLine}" Value="">
                                <Setter Property="Visibility" Value="Collapsed" />
                            </DataTrigger>

                            <!--
                                RED WHILE THIS SESSION HAS NO ADMINISTRATOR RIGHTS, 2026-09-02, on
                                the owner's words that without them this window is for looking at.
                                Amber says "watch out" and the truth is "you cannot act", which is
                                a boundary rather than a caution. That still holds - for the rights
                                sentence, which is the first run above and red by itself.

                                THE WHOLE LINE WAS RED UNTIL 2026-09-23, AND THE REASON GIVEN FOR IT
                                WAS NOT TRUE. It said the other notes on this line were all about a
                                list incomplete for the reason the first note gives. The sentence
                                about folded copies is not about incompleteness at all, and the
                                sentences about a reading in progress are not about rights - so a
                                red line said "refused" about things nobody refused (UX-GUI-009).
                                The line was split into runs, which is the cost that note named, and
                                the trigger that coloured all of it is gone.
                            -->
                        </Style.Triggers>
                    </Style>
                </TextBlock.Style>
            </TextBlock>

            <Button Grid.Column="1"
                    x:Name="ElevateButton"
                    AutomationProperties.AutomationId="elevate">
                <Button.Style>
                    <Style TargetType="Button" BasedOn="{StaticResource ElevateOffer}">
                        <Setter Property="Visibility" Value="Collapsed" />
                        <Style.Triggers>
                            <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding Says.NotElevated}" Value="True">
                                <Setter Property="Visibility" Value="Visible" />
                            </DataTrigger>
                        </Style.Triggers>
                    </Style>
                </Button.Style>
            </Button>
        </Grid>

        <TextBlock Text="{Binding Says.Problem}" TextWrapping="Wrap">
            <TextBlock.Style>
                <Style TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource ProblemText}">
                    <Style.Triggers>
                        <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding Says.Problem}" Value="">
                            <Setter Property="Visibility" Value="Collapsed" />
                        </DataTrigger>
                    </Style.Triggers>
                </Style>
            </TextBlock.Style>
        </TextBlock>
    </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
